The zip module assembles a ZIP archive on the fly from files that nginx
fetches itself.  An upstream answers a request with a list of files, their
sizes and checksums, and the module streams the archive to the client
without ever writing it to disk.  Ranges and resumed downloads work as long
as the upstream keeps the list stable.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built by
the nginx ports when their HTTP_ZIP option is enabled.
